## User-facing decisions

Interviewed with the navigator on 2026-08-18 over
`.cerebro/scratch/ah-dwk6-idle-units.html`, in two rounds. The chosen mockup is committed to
`docs/ui/ah-dwk6-idle-units.html`. **The mockup's §1 carries the measurement the decisions were made
against** — 2 of 27 units on the real turn-71 template — and is worth reading before changing any of
them.

**Q1 — which units are exempt.** Chosen: **none, and the check is on by default.** Rejected:
*off by default* like `hex-unguarded` (a check nobody switches on never catches the unit you forgot);
*exempt an empty block* as deliberate silence (silent on the real turn and needs no test changed, but
a forgotten unit also has an empty block, so it misses the case the bead exists for); and a per-unit
**"intentionally idle" mark** (the only thing that really distinguishes parked from forgotten, but a
new persisted per-unit setting and a new control — roughly triples the bead). The navigator was shown
that A warns about two units on their own real turn, every turn, and chose it anyway.

**Q2 — units on GUARD.** Chosen: **warn like any other unit.** GUARD is a flag rather than a month's
work — a guard can tax as well — so a garrison that could be earning is worth being told about.
Rejected: exempting guards, which adds a special case to a one-sentence rule.

**Q3 — the wording.** Chosen: **`has no order that spends the month`**. It states the rule, so the
player knows what would silence it, and stays neutral about whether it was deliberate. Rejected:
`does nothing this month` (shorter, but accusing about a unit parked on purpose) and
`is idle this month` (`IDLE` is itself an Atlantis order, so it reads as though the unit was told to
be idle).

**Q4 — the Warnings tab.** Chosen: the existing **Orders** group, entry **"Units that do nothing"** /
**"A unit with no order that spends its month."** Rejected: a new "The month" group for a single
check.

**Q5 — a unit with no block in the document at all.** Chosen: **warn, with no line.** A deleted block
is still a unit doing nothing, and the finding shows in the region pane and the problems panel where
a player would scan for it. Rejected: warning only about units that have a block, which would keep
every finding anchored but let a deleted block escape.

**Q6 — CAST, asked during the amendment (2026-08-19).** The rules say CAST is not a full month order,
but the same classifier feeds `is_busy` and so the shipped `teacher-has-free-slots` warning. Chosen:
**free for the new check only** — `spends_the_month` follows the rules, `is_busy` keeps its CAST
exception, so no shipped warning changes. Rejected: following the rules everywhere (correct, but adds
spare-teacher findings on every casting mage) and keeping CAST month-long (the false negative that
failed the verification). The navigator added, unprompted, that *"teaching warning should only be on
units actually TEACHing this month. Only warn if they have free slots. Not someone not teaching"* —
filed as **`ah-vw63`**, which is where the exception above should be removed.

**Q7 — the two orders the rules never place, asked during the amendment.** Chosen by the navigator
directly: **TRANSPORT and DISTRIBUTE are free; ANNIHILATE is month-long.** That empties the
"uncertain" category entirely, so the only unjudgeable lines left are keywords the app does not
recognise at all.

**Q8 — an unrecognised keyword.** Not put to the navigator, and it should be said plainly: a unit
holding a keyword in neither list — a typo, or an order added to the game after this list — raises
**nothing**. It is the conservative direction, and the syntax checker already flags a typo
separately. If the navigator would rather see a warning there, it is a one-line change to this rule
and a new message to agree.

**Not asked, and deliberately so:** the exhaustive-`match` classifier and the `is_busy` refactor
(architecture), and recording unread lines (architecture). **Also not asked, and the reason this plan
needed amending: the *scope* of the unread rule.** It was presented in the mockup's §5 as a piece of
architecture, and it was the whole defect. The navigator was told about the unread-line
problem in the mockup's §5 so the silence it buys is not a surprise, but the mechanism was not put to
them as a choice.

## Out of scope

